# Testing conventions

- Normal tests and CI are deterministic, secret-free, and network-free. They
  never call Groq or any live service.
- Use only Fake, Replay, finite synthetic fixtures, or an injected fake HTTP
  transport around Live-Groq.
- Do not create a fourth provider for tests and do not place real-provider calls
  in a `test` directory or test command.
- Use fixed logical time, seeded/deterministic IDs, and exact structural
  assertions. Avoid wall-clock timing and model-graded expectations.
- Derive CV expectations by reading `content/source/cv.yaml` at test time.
  Never commit a copied snapshot containing résumé/contact text.
- Cover strict schema rejection, exact résumé leaf coverage, Rego allow/deny,
  deny-without-tool, event order, manifest digest mismatch, generated drift,
  and secret boundaries.
- Mutate event body, sequence, proof sibling, and root; each integrity check
  must fail.
- Serve E2E from the final static directory with only the local origin allowed.
  Direct-load every required physical route.
- Test keyboard operation, text-plus-shape states, no-JavaScript content,
  reduced motion, zoom/reflow, and automated WCAG 2.2 AA checks.
- A manual Live diagnostic is operational tooling only: it is never a merge
  gate, evaluation, golden updater, or substitute for transport fixtures.
